              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a seat belt, then the Arabic for a crew."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: مضيف",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مضيف — muḍīf — \"a flight attendant; a host\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أحضر المضيف كوب ماء لأمي. aḥḍara al-muḍīf kūb māʾ li-ummī. The flight attendant brought my mother a cup of water."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A woman is muḍīfa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مضيف (muḍīf) is built on the native Arabic root ḍ-y-f, \"to be a guest\" (Lane). It is the Form IV participle, \"one who takes in guests\": a host, and on a plane a flight attendant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
